cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "imagewright: Image Generation Over One HTTP Contract"
abstract: >
  imagewright generates images from text prompts through one HTTP contract,
  /v1/images/generations. It provides a Python client and command line that
  choose a backend in a fixed order (a named or configured server, a local
  server found by discovery, or FLUX.2 Klein loaded in process), an OpenAI
  backend, local servers for FLUX.2 Klein (mflux, Apple Silicon) and
  SDXL-Lightning (diffusers, CUDA, MPS or CPU) that answer the contract, and
  an MCP server whose tool returns a generated image under the client's size
  limit. It depends on no knowledge graph package.
